<LegalLayout title="KVKK / Personal Data" updated="August 2026">

<p>This page serves as our disclosure text ("Aydınlatma Metni") under the Turkish Personal Data Protection Law No. 6698 ("KVKK"), informing you as the data subject about how <strong>Cappadocia Kaphera Travel Agency</strong> (TÜRSAB No: 18577), acting as the data controller, processes your personal data.</p>

<h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
<p>Cappadocia Kaphera Travel Agency, trading as CappadociaGo, based in Cappadocia, Nevşehir, Türkiye, acts as the "Data Controller" (Veri Sorumlusu) as defined under KVKK Article 3, for personal data collected through our website, WhatsApp line, and booking processes.</p>

<h2>2. Categories of Personal Data Processed</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Identity data:</strong> name, surname, nationality, and where legally required for certain activities (e.g. balloon flight manifests), date of birth and ID/passport number.</li>
  <li><strong>Contact data:</strong> phone number, email address, accommodation address in Cappadocia.</li>
  <li><strong>Transaction data:</strong> booking history, payment records (excluding full card numbers), invoices.</li>
  <li><strong>Digital footprint data:</strong> IP address, cookies, and website usage data (see our <a href="/legal/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>).</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Purpose of Processing</h2>
<p>Your personal data is processed for the purposes of: preparing and managing your tour reservation; coordinating hotel pickup with our operating partners; fulfilling legal obligations towards aviation and tourism authorities; issuing invoices and fulfilling tax obligations; responding to your requests and complaints; and, where you consent, sending you information about our tours and offers.</p>

<h2>4. Method and Legal Basis of Collection</h2>
<p>Your data is collected through our website's booking forms, WhatsApp conversations, email correspondence, and — for in-person bookings — directly from you at the point of sale. This data is processed based on the legal grounds set out in KVKK Article 5, namely: it being expressly permitted by law, being necessary for the establishment or performance of a contract, being necessary for compliance with our legal obligations, and, where applicable, your explicit consent.</p>

<h2>5. Transfer of Personal Data</h2>
<p>In line with KVKK Articles 8 and 9, your personal data may be transferred, to the extent necessary for the purposes above, to: tour operators and suppliers who deliver the booked service; payment institutions; and competent public authorities where legally required. Where any transfer occurs outside Türkiye, we take reasonable steps to ensure an equivalent level of protection.</p>

<h2>6. Your Rights as a Data Subject</h2>
<p>Under KVKK Article 11, you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Learn whether your personal data is being processed;</li>
  <li>Request information if it has been processed;</li>
  <li>Learn the purpose of processing and whether it is used accordingly;</li>
  <li>Know the third parties to whom your data is transferred, domestically or abroad;</li>
  <li>Request correction of incomplete or inaccurate data;</li>
  <li>Request deletion or destruction of your data, subject to legal retention obligations;</li>
  <li>Object to a result that is against you, arising from analysis of your data exclusively through automated systems;</li>
  <li>Request compensation for damages arising from unlawful processing of your data.</li>
</ul>

<div class="highlight-box">
  <strong>How to submit a request:</strong> You may exercise these rights by emailing <a href="mailto:info@kapheratravel.com">info@kapheratravel.com</a> with the subject line "KVKK Request", including your full name and a description of your request. We will respond within the timeframe required by KVKK (generally within 30 days).
</div>

<h2>7. Data Security Measures</h2>
<p>We implement reasonable administrative and technical safeguards to prevent unlawful access, disclosure, alteration or destruction of personal data, in accordance with KVKK Article 12.</p>

</LegalLayout>
